    "definition": "Twelve arbitrary distinct rational points in the plane minimize maximum squared pair distance divided by minimum squared pair distance. No collinearity or bounding-box constraint. Density and continuity preserve the real-coordinate infimum.",
    "primary_source": "Friedman maxmin n12 page attributes Rechenberg2006 value5+2sqrt3 without optimality proof. Root read the source diagram and independently reconstructed Q(sqrt3) coordinates: all66 pairs have minimum squared distance1 and maximum5+2sqrt3, with21 minimum pairs. Exact rational approximation to sqrt3 yields the formally reproduced slightly weaker ratio; it is not identified with the exact irrational record.",
    "independent_method": "For each of five saved witnesses, rebuild all66 distances via the rational Gram identity norm(i)+norm(j)-2dot(i,j), separate from formal coordinate differences, and divide exact maximum by positive minimum.",
    "open_status": "AlphaEvolve2511.02864v1 section6.50 distinguishes proved n<=8 from numerical n9..30 candidates. Later improvements at16/21/22/29 do not settle12; no n12 optimality proof located in reviewed sources.",
    "admission": "Initial grid13, independent traditional/evolution48625/5274, human/reference rational near8.4641016151. All five strict runs, damage, claim invariance, independent exact score, replay, cold export and all failure controls pass. Agent16tests passed; main shared run follows."
  }
